Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: add QJL/Polar/TBQ CPU kernels and quantize
 functions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Copy CPU kernel files from elizaOS fork and wire into CMakeLists.txt:

  ggml-cpu/qjl/          — QJL 1-bit JL-sketch quantize + score kernels
                           (ref, AVX2, AVX-VNNI, NEON, DOTPROD dispatchers)
  ggml-cpu/polarquant/   — PolarQuant pre-Hadamard-transposed dot kernels
                           (ref, AVX2, NEON + runtime dispatcher)
  ggml-cpu/fused-attn-qjl-tbq*  — fused QJL-K + TBQ-V attention (ref, AVX2, NEON)
  ggml-cpu/fused-q4-polar-dot*  — fused Q4_POLAR dot product (ref, AVX2, NEON)
  ggml-cpu/fused-hadamard-polar-dot.c — Hadamard-rotated PolarQuant dot
  ggml-cpu/attn-score-tbq-polar.c — scalar ref for ATTN_SCORE_TBQ/POLAR ops
  ggml-cpu/quants-polar.c — PolarQuant CPU quant/dequant support

Add to ggml-quants.{h,c}:
  - TBQ3/4 0/K, TBQ3_TCQ, QJL1_256, Q4_POLAR quantize_row_*_ref
  - Corresponding dequantize_row_* functions
  - Bulk quantize_* entry points
  - TBQ helper statics (codebooks, preconditioner, Hadamard, K-block rotation)
  - TCQ-3 Viterbi encoder + 9-bit sliding-window decoder
  - PolarQuant Q4 Lloyd-Max + QJL residual encoder/decoder
  - ggml_q4_polar_{set,get}_use_qjl runtime toggle

Wire type_traits to_float/from_float_ref pointers (0026 left them NULL).
Add quantize_chunk switch cases for all 7 new types.

Also adds: polar_centroids.h, ggml-tcq-codebook.h (lookup tables).

SIMD dispatch defines (QJL_HAVE_*, POLARQUANT_HAVE_*) propagated via CMake
based on GGML_AVX2 / GGML_SYSTEM_ARCH settings.
